-- Cause: our smart_scripts for these entries come from the alexkulya import (identical to ref_alex) or are missing; the Cataclysm sniff data (ref_cpp) has SmartAI with the retail casts for them.
-- Change: port the ref_cpp SmartAI (smart_scripts source_type 0 + 8 timed action lists + waypoints + conditions) for 25 creatures (14 new, 11 replacing an unchanged alexkulya script); AIName set to SmartAI for 14 entries that had none.
-- Schema/enum mapping: target_param4 = 0; event_flags 512 (WHILE_CHARMED in TC master; RAID40 difficulty in our core, would disable the event) dropped, 256 -> 0x10000 (DONT_RESET); action 27 COMBAT_STOP -> 203, 85 SELF_CAST -> 11 CAST with flag 0x10, 134 INVOKER_CAST -> 85; cast triggerFlags/targetsLimit (param3/4) = 0.
-- Source: ref_cpp (Cataclysm Preservation Project TDB434.22011, sniff-based) smart_scripts/creature_text/waypoints/conditions, rows copied 1:1 apart from the mapping above. Every spell id checked against the 5.4.8 client Spell.dbc + SpellEffect.dbc on dev (exists, has effects, name matches the ref_cpp comment). Not yet seen in game.
-- Rollback: rollback/405_batch8_rollback.sql (re-inserts the 11 replaced old scripts, deletes the ported rows, resets AIName for the 14 entries that had none).
-- Rollback (short, loses the replaced old scripts of 16929,19414,16967,19350,16968,16974,19349,16975,19305,20748,20483): DELETE FROM smart_scripts WHERE source_type=0 AND entryorguid IN (16929,22323,19414,16967,19350,16968,16974,19349,16975,18733,18969,19305,22038,22452,23188,11980,22106,20747,20748,22499,21319,20402,20403,20454,20483); DELETE FROM smart_scripts WHERE source_type=9 AND entryorguid IN (1198000,1198001,2203800,2245200,2318800,2318801,2318802,2318803); UPDATE creature_template SET AIName='' WHERE entry IN (22323,18733,18969,22038,22452,23188,11980,22106,20747,22499,21319,20402,20403,20454);

